<section xml:id="section-20" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Applications of Double Integrals</title>
 <introduction>
    <p>
      In this final section we will look at a few applications. First we will look at integrating using polar coordinates, which is not technically an application but 
      polar coordinates are often used in physics and engineering applications to simplify calculations. Then we will look at calculating center of mass before wrapping 
      up with a few more application examples.
    </p>
  </introduction>
  <objectives>
    <title>Applications of Double Integrals</title>
     <introduction>

    <p>
    In this section we will look at:
    </p>

  </introduction>

